// @emit-error only i32[] arrays and struct/union element arrays are supported
// THE WITNESS FOR A GATE THAT WAS BRIEFLY OPENED BY THE WRONG PREDICATE.
// `structIdxOfElemName`'s trailing gate asks `nameIsStructDecl(sNames[si])` — is the row
// a declared STRUCT — and its header records why it must stay a loud REJECT: admitting a
// shape-armed union routes it into the union-arm narrow machinery, whose read side still
// mis-lowers that flow.
//
// A destringify slice replaced that call with the `sRowDecl` column, which banks
// `cUserTypes.has(nm)` at the mint. The two are NOT the same question: `cUserTypes` holds
// UNION declarations too, while `nameIsStructDecl` requires a `TypeDecl` node. A
// canonicalized object intersection is a one-variant `UnionDecl` interned as a struct row
// by `internShapeAs(s.udName, …)` — so its name is in `cUserTypes`, is not a `TypeDecl`,
// and the column opened the gate the scan had closed. This file compiled and ran under
// that slice; it must reject.
//
// The dual-run that licensed the swap read 1,029 agree / 0 disagree and was simply blind:
// no corpus file paired a struct-alias union with an inline spelling of its own shape.
// This is that file.
//
// RE-MEASURED 2026-08-28 (silent-class-inventory D402), and the stated harm did NOT
